Name a shifted symbol's keystroke without shift

A browser reports a shifted symbol key by the symbol it types, `?` for shift
and `/`, with shift still held, so the keystroke reads shift-? and a binding of
`?` never matches it. gpui's Linux platform names such a keystroke without
shift, keeping shift only on a key whose character has case; naming the
browser's keystrokes the same way lets one keymap serve both.

